<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Land of Confusion - Syria, 2021</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;CMO: "Land of Confusion" - The Syrian Missile Crisis, 2021&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;Al "Beirutdude" Sandrik&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;The Time Is: 13 March 2021 10:00:00 Zulu/12:00:00 Damascus Time&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;Last Edited: 1 November 2020&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;Israel/Lebanon/Syria&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;Playable as Israel&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;Up to 18 Hours Duration (See Notes)&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;　&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;Background: &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;Iran, through the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps ( IRGC ), has been building permanent bases in Syria as the price for its support in the Syrian Civil War. Included in those facilities are Surface to Surface Missile (SSM) bases/production facilities and Surface to Air Missile ( SAM ), Anti-Access/Area Denial ( A2AD ) systems that Israel has continually indicated it will not allow to be deployed in Syria. Repeatedly the Israeli Defense Forces ( IDF )&lt;STRONG&gt;/&lt;/STRONG&gt;Israeli Air Force ( IAF ) have hit Iranian targets in northwest Syria. Most notably on July, 20th, 2020 the IAF hit as many as 70 targets including missile facilities near Masyaf, Syria. By September/October, 2020 the IRGC was working on reconstituting that ability. &lt;EM&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;This is where we diverge from, history&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;…　&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;November, 2020; An Iranian Bavar ( S-300 clone ) SAM/A2AD system and Mersad ( Improved Hawks ) were set up near the Masyaf Missile Facility and additional&amp;nbsp;Mersads near the, under construction, SSM facility in Wadi Jahannam, Syria ( NW of Masyaf ).　&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;December, 2020; Iranian Fatah A SSMs are identified in the Masyaf SSM Facility at launch sites in the northern portion of the facility.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;January, 2021: The, until this point ineffective, Syrian S-300 battalion sited near Masyaf is moved to Damascus International Airport to stiffen Syrian A2AD in the southern portion of the country. Russian "Advisors" completely turn the unit over to Syrian control.　&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;February 2021: Russian President Putin, noting growing concerns over IAF attacks in Syria, repeatedly warns the Israelis over, "any attacks on Russian property in Syria." His wording seems to imply that it applies to ground facilities and naval vessels. Russian aircraft continue to intercept and observe IAF aircraft over northern Lebanon and northwest Syria with several "mock dogfights" ( without an exchange of weapons ) ensuing.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;Early March, 2021: Human Intelligence ( HUMINT ) indicates that Sector 4 of the Center for Syrian Studies and Research (&amp;nbsp;SSRC ) continued working with the IRGC and Hezbollah in fitting chemical warheads to rockets and missiles and especially the Iranian Fatah A Medium Range Ballistic Missiles ( MRBMs ). The Israeli Cabinet decides on action to destroy the Syrian research facility, the IRGC SSM facilities and MRBMs in a massive attack.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;11 March 2021: With a "New Moon" period approaching Syrian ADA/A2AD systems go on high alert…　&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;NOTES: &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;1. Israeli/IAF/IDF Side postures:&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; a. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;Hezbollah, Syria, &amp;amp; Iran – "&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT color=red&gt;Hostile&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;"&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; b. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;Russia &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;– "&lt;FONT color=#008000&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Neutral&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;"&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; c. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;United States - "&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT color=blue&gt;Friendly&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;"&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;d. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT face="Courier New"&gt;&lt;FONT face="Courier New"&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;Civilians – "&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT color=green&gt;Neutral&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;"&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;2. Your target areas are marked with References Points, feel free to delete them once you know where you need to hit. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;3. Each Iranian Missile TEL represents a single launcher/missile with no reloads.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;4. Your aircraft have no loadouts, &lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;U&gt;you&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;, decide your strike package! 2 options:&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; a. Ready them &amp;amp; run the scenario in compressed time until 16:00 UTC/18:00 Local. ( 6 hours longer intel on target areas )&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; b. Ready in the Scenario Editor and also&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; i. Change start time to 16:00:00 UTC&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; ii. Change scenario duration to 12 hours.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;5. You gain Victory Points ( VPs ) for destroying Iranian and ( &lt;EM&gt;&lt;U&gt;some&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/EM&gt; ) Syrian facilities. The SSM facilities and the Syrian SSRC lab are your primary ( VP gaining ) targets, the ADA/A2AD system and fighters are what you need to&amp;nbsp;neutralize to get at them.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;6. Israel is averse to losses, sorry but it is! They will if they absolutely need to ( Yom Kippur War ) but every loss is deeply felt! Losing IAF aircraft will result in the, substantial, loss of Israeli VPs. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;7. Civilians, there are civilian aircraft in the area, &lt;EM&gt;please avoid killing them! &lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;8. This is the "Land of Confusion" ( sorry &lt;EM&gt;Genesis &lt;/EM&gt;! ), Hezbollah, Syria, Iran,&amp;nbsp;and Russia are all present, they are "Friendly" with each other but each operates autonomously. So, Russia’s ADA radars are providing info to Syria but may not attack IAF aircraft ( unless something goes bad ). Oh BTW Israel may receive some USAF AEW/ELINT support. Confused yet?&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;9. AGAIN, &lt;U&gt;&lt;EM&gt;KNOW WHAT YOU ARE ATTACKING&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/U&gt;. Destroying Russian ADA or other facilities/vessels WILL bring Russia into the battle,&amp;nbsp;Russia has been clear on this point! Conversely, it is POSSIBLE to "dogfight" investigating Russian fighters without Russia coming in as an active belligerant or not!&amp;nbsp;So they may attack you or&amp;nbsp;they may not, depends upon the pilots. Conversely, Syrian fighters ARE hostile! Confused?&amp;nbsp;Oy Vey! &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;10. I have very carefully found and ID'ed the Russian ADA sites on &lt;EM&gt;Google Earth&lt;/EM&gt;. The S-300/400 ( sources vary, I assumed S-400 for the scenario ) battalion in the Syrian mountains northeast of Masyaf IS THERE trust me!&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;11. The Syrian S-300 Battery is a bit of a mystery. Some say it is under Syrian control and they just can’t handle it well. Some say the Russians are not allowing it to fire on IAF aircraft. I have seen Satellite imagery of it near Masyaf but descriptions of a system near Damascus are also out there. Scenario wise, with the Iranian Bavar SAM systems set up near Masyaf&amp;nbsp;a Syrian S-300 becomes somewhat redundant there. Thus, I assumed the Russians turned&amp;nbsp;the S-300&amp;nbsp;completely over to Syrian control and it was moved south to cover Damascus.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;12. All of the SAM WRA ranges have been set to &lt;U&gt;&lt;EM&gt;NOT&lt;STRONG&gt; fire &lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/U&gt;at aircraft over either Syria ( for IDF SAMs )&amp;nbsp;or Israel ( for Syrian/Iranian/Russian SAMs ). As the Israeli player you might want to change that once missiles start to fly, but you do risk shooting down a Russian aircraft if you do. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;13. There is an Exclusion Zone available over Israel and &lt;EM&gt;&lt;U&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;any&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/EM&gt; aircraft ( I.e. Russian or Civilian ) becomes hostile if it overflies Israel if you turn the "Aircraft" setting on. Right now it is disabled for aircraft because it will make civilian airliners hostile. I originally set it up to help the AI and then decided it wasn't necessary, but left it in as a player option.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;14. Please have your Pop Up windows activated.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;　&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;Originally created under &lt;STRONG&gt;CMO Version 1.01, Build 1147.14 – Data Base: DB3000 487&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;.INI and .Delta files have both been provided for deep rebuilds&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;Al "BeirutDude" Sandrik ( ex-Beachinnole )&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT color=blue face="Microsoft Sans Serif"&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Al.Sandrik@gmail.com&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
